{"ts": "2026-09-25T18:20:23Z", "kind": "tool_return", "run_step": 9, "tool_call_id": "toolu_01QYnPG38eC1rqvYkxpP9ykb", "tool_name": "record_progress", "args": {"thread": "C-1042 / SUP-5601 & SUP-5602 billing escalation", "stage": "RECONCILING", "note": "Findings confirmed: (1) Deep Time Analytics $30 add-on legitimate, added by admin U-2 (SE-6) per POL-B-ADD, started at renewal, billed separately on INV-2609-AO - not an error, just unexplained to owner (who is a different user, U-1, than the admin who added it, U-2). (2) July $59.60 upgrade charge (INV-2607P/TX-8702) is correct proration per POL-B-PRO; SUP-5549 agent correctly said no additional credit due on THAT invoice, but separately CR-778 ($19.60 unused-time credit) was properly issued same day and remains unapplied - owner not notified (owner_notified:false) and CR-778 is sitting unapplied because SUP-5390 disabled auto-apply. This isn't an error but is an unresolved/pending action - customer entitled to have it applied on request. (3) 'Duplicate' $149 charge on 9/14 (TX-9001 & TX-9002): TX-9002 was an authorization that hit capture_timeout, retried as TX-9001 which settled; TX-9002 was never captured and was released 2026-09-18. Only ONE actual settlement (TX-9001) posted to INV-2609. This is NOT a duplicate charge - it's a single payment with a retried authorization, consistent with processor record. However, S-22 in SUP-5601 PROMISED a $149 refund within 5-7 business days, calling it a duplicate - this is an incorrect commitment since no duplicate charge occurred and per POL-B-REF support agents may not promise refunds before billing review. S-05 in SUP-5602 already flagged refund NOT yet issued, pending investigation - good, but the erroneous promise to customer needs correction/withdrawal.", "open_questions": ["Should CR-778 be applied to an invoice now given customer's manual-apply preference (SUP-5390) - needs customer request or billing specialist decision", "Need to withdraw/correct the erroneous 'duplicate charge' refund promise from SUP-5601 (S-22) since TX-9002 was an uncaptured/released authorization, not a real duplicate charge", "Should owner (U-1) be proactively notified about the Deep Time Analytics add-on added by admin U-2, and about unapplied CR-778 credit?"]}, "category": "note", "effect": "none", "result": {"synthetic": true, "recorded": true}}
